  "text": "Buxton Veterinary Oncology | Cancer Treatment for Dogs\nSkip to Main Content\nSkip to Footer\nCAREERS\n|\nDownload Our App\nHours\n47959 North Carolina Hwy 12\nBuxton, NC 27920\n(252) 995-3960\nAbout Us\nOur Practice\nMeet the Team\nKitty Hawk Location\nCareers\nPolicies & Payments\nClose\nServices\nAll Services\nDog & Cat Care\nPocket Pet Care\nExotic Pet Care\nPet Dental Care\nSurgical Procedures\nPet Microchipping\nDiagnostics\nEquine Care\nPet Laser Therapy\nPet Behavior Counseling\nCanine Reproduction\nPet Nutrition\nPharmacy & Pet Products\nPet Health Certificates\nOphthalmology\nPet Chemotherapy\nPet Emergencies\nClose\nContact\nContact\nBook an Appointment\nClient Forms\nRefill Request\nClose\nPet Corner\nTips for Beach Dogs\nWhat to Expect\nNews & Articles\nResources & Links\nClose\nBook an Appointment\nBook an Appointment\nCall: (252) 995-3960\nHours\nAbout Us\nOur Practice\nMeet the Team\nKitty Hawk Location\nCareers\nPolicies & Payments\nClose\nServices\nAll Services\nDog & Cat Care\nPocket Pet Care\nExotic Pet Care\nPet Dental Care\nSurgical Procedures\nPet Microchipping\nDiagnostics\nEquine Care\nPet Laser Therapy\nPet Behavior Counseling\nCanine Reproduction\nPet Nutrition\nPharmacy & Pet Products\nPet Health Certificates\nOphthalmology\nPet Chemotherapy\nPet Emergencies\nClose\nContact\nContact\nBook an Appointment\nClient Forms\nRefill Request\nClose\nPet Corner\nTips for Beach Dogs\nWhat to Expect\nNews & Articles\nResources & Links\nClose\nDownload Our App\nCareers\nPet Chemotherapy\nHelp your pet live the life they deserve.\nIf your pet has been diagnosed with cancer, chemotherapy may be an option for them. At Coastal Animal Hospital of Hatteras Island, we can discuss treatment options including chemotherapy. Chemotherapy can slow the spread of cancer, shrink tumors prior to surgery, and buy precious time with terminally ill pets.\nHow does chemotherapy work?\nChemotherapy drugs attack cancer cells in pets the same way they attack cancer cells in people. Protocols vary from pet to pet and are determined based upon the type of cancer, the stage of the cancer, the pet’s current health, and their medical history. Prior to starting chemotherapy, your veterinarian will go over your pet’s treatment options and discuss any potential side effects.\nAdministering a single dose of chemotherapy is relatively quick and easy. We offer both on-site injections and take-home oral medications. The number of chemotherapy treatments your pet will need is based upon the type of cancer they have, their response to treatment, and the specific treatment goals you and your veterinarian have created. Pets who go into remission will be able to taper off their treatments, but others may require chemotherapy for the remainder of their life.\nIf you have questions about chemotherapy or would like to schedule a consultation, please call us at\n(252) 995-3960\n.\nCoastal Animal Hospital of Hatteras Island\n47959 North Carolina Hwy 12 Buxton, NC 27920\nemail: hatterasisland@coastalanimalhospital.com\nphone: (252) 995-3960\nfax: (252) 995-3300\nServing the Buxton, NC area including (but not limited to): Avon, Frisco, Hatteras, Manteo, Ocracoke, Rodanthe, Salvo, and Tri-Villages.\nOffice Hours\nMonday:\n8:00am  - 5:30pm\nTuesday:\n8:00am  - 5:30pm\nWednesday:\nClosed\nThursday:\n8:00am  - 5:30pm\nFriday:\n8:00am  - 5:30pm\nSaturday:\nClosed\nSunday:\nClosed\nFor immediate veterinary care outside of our business hours >\nView our holiday hours and closings >\ncareers\n© 2026 Coastal Animal Hospital of Hatteras Island. All rights reserved.\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nTerms & Conditions\nModal title\n×\nCras mattis consectetur purus sit amet fermentum. Cras justo odio, dapibus ac facilisis in, egestas eget quam. Morbi leo risus, porta ac consectetur ac, vestibulum at eros.\nClose\nSave changes\nGoogle Recaptcha",
